        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ complete the square:\n\n$$\nx=- t^{2} - 2 t - 5=- \\left(t + 1\\right)^{2} - 4 .\n$$\n\nThe vertex parameter is $t=-1$, which is admissible. The vertex value is $-4$ and is attained. The coordinate is unbounded below. Consequently, $x\\le -4.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ complete the square:\n\n$$\ny=t^{2} - 6 t + 5=\\left(t - 3\\right)^{2} - 4 .\n$$\n\nThe vertex parameter is $t=3$, which is admissible. The vertex value is $-4$ and is attained. The coordinate is unbounded above. Consequently, $y\\ge -4.$",
